    sampleAnswer: "Direct answer:\n\nThese JPA annotations let you model a value object (a group of fields with no independent identity/lifecycle of its own) as part of a parent entity's table, instead of creating a separate entity and table. @Embeddable marks a class as embeddable \u2014 it has no @Id of its own. @Embedded is placed on the field in the owning entity to include that embeddable object's fields inline within the owning entity's table. This is useful for grouping logically related fields (like an Address made of street, city, zip) without the overhead of a full separate table and join.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```java\n@Embeddable public class Address {\n    private String street;\n    private String city;\n    private String zip;\n}\n@Entity public class Employee {\n    @Id\n    @GeneratedValue private Long id;\n    @Embedded private Address address;\n    // street, city, zip columns get added directly to the Employee table\n}\n```",
