    sampleAnswer: "Direct answer:\n\nAn object-level lock (acquired via synchronized on an instance method or a synchronized(this) block) locks the specific object instance, so different threads working on different instances of the class don't block each other \u2014 only threads accessing the same instance are serialized. A class-level lock (acquired via a static synchronized method, or synchronized(ClassName.class)) locks the Class object itself, which is shared across all instances, meaning it prevents concurrent execution of that synchronized static logic across ALL instances and even across different threads regardless of which object they're using.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```java\nclass Counter {\n    private int count = 0;\n    private static int totalInstancesCreated = 0;\n    public synchronized void increment() {\n        count++;\n    }\n    // object-level lock, per-instance\n    public static synchronized void incrementTotal() {\n        totalInstancesCreated++;\n    }\n    //\n    class-level lock, shared across all instances\n}\n```",
    detailedAnswer: "Direct answer:\n\nAn object-level lock (acquired via synchronized on an instance method or a synchronized(this) block) locks the specific object instance, so different threads working on different instances of the class don't block each other \u2014 only threads accessing the same instance are serialized. A class-level lock (acquired via a static synchronized method, or synchronized(ClassName.class)) locks the Class object itself, which is shared across all instances, meaning it prevents concurrent execution of that synchronized static logic across ALL instances and even across different threads regardless of which object they're using.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```java\nclass Counter {\n    private int count = 0;\n    private static int totalInstancesCreated = 0;\n    public synchronized void increment() {\n        count++;\n    }\n    // object-level lock, per-instance\n    public static synchronized void incrementTotal() {\n        totalInstancesCreated++;\n    }\n    //\n    class-level lock, shared across all instances\n}\n```",
