    sampleAnswer: "Direct answer:\n\nA derived query method lets you define a repository query simply by following a naming convention in the method signature \u2014 Spring Data JPA parses the method name, extracts the property names and keywords (like findBy, And, Or, GreaterThan, OrderBy), and automatically generates the corresponding JPQL/SQL query at runtime, without you writing any query code at all. This works well for simple to moderately complex queries; for more complex logic, you'd fall back to @Query with JPQL or native SQL, or the Criteria API/Specifications.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```sql\npublic interface EmployeeRepository extends JpaRepository<Employee, Long> {\n  List<Employee> findByLastNameAndDepartment(String lastName, String department);\n  // Spring Data JPA automatically generates:\n  //\n\nSELECT e\n  FROM Employee e\n  WHERE e.lastName = ?1 AND e.department = ?2 List<Employee> findBySalaryGreaterThanOrderBySalaryDesc(double minSalary);\n  // Generates:\n\nSELECT e\n  FROM Employee e\n  WHERE e.salary > ?1\n  ORDER BY e.salary DESC\n  }\n```",
    detailedAnswer: "Direct answer:\n\nA derived query method lets you define a repository query simply by following a naming convention in the method signature \u2014 Spring Data JPA parses the method name, extracts the property names and keywords (like findBy, And, Or, GreaterThan, OrderBy), and automatically generates the corresponding JPQL/SQL query at runtime, without you writing any query code at all. This works well for simple to moderately complex queries; for more complex logic, you'd fall back to @Query with JPQL or native SQL, or the Criteria API/Specifications.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```sql\npublic interface EmployeeRepository extends JpaRepository<Employee, Long> {\n  List<Employee> findByLastNameAndDepartment(String lastName, String department);\n  // Spring Data JPA automatically generates:\n  //\n\nSELECT e\n  FROM Employee e\n  WHERE e.lastName = ?1 AND e.department = ?2 List<Employee> findBySalaryGreaterThanOrderBySalaryDesc(double minSalary);\n  // Generates:\n\nSELECT e\n  FROM Employee e\n  WHERE e.salary > ?1\n  ORDER BY e.salary DESC\n  }\n```",
